              "scriptOrigin": "script-docx",
              "script": "So let’s talk about renewable energy sources. This is an increasingly important topic as we look for alternatives to fossil fuels coal, oil, and natural gas. Renewable energy comes from sources that are naturally replenished and won’t run out.\nSolar energy is one of the most common types. It captures sunlight using panels and converts it into electricity. The sun provides an enormous amount of energy every day, far more than humans currently use. The challenge is that solar power depends on weather conditions and doesn’t work at night without storage systems.\nWind energy is another major source. Wind turbines convert the movement of air into electrical power. Wind farms can be built on land or offshore, and they produce no pollution during operation. However, wind is variable; sometimes it blows strongly, sometimes not at all.\nHydroelectric power uses flowing water to generate electricity. Dams are built on rivers, and the moving water spins turbines. This is reliable and produces large amounts of power, but building dams can affect river ecosystems and displace communities.\nEach renewable source has advantages and limitations. That’s why many experts believe the future lies in combining multiple sources. By using solar, wind, and water power together, we can create a more reliable and sustainable system."
